d parmhet: Heterogeneity tests in parmest resultssets
d parmhet and parmiv are designed for use with parmest resultssets,
d which have one observation per estimated parameter and data on
d parameter estimates.  parmhet inputs variables containing parameter
d estimates, standard errors and (optionally) degrees of freedom, and
d outputs an output dataset (or resultsset) with one observation, or one
d observation per by-group, and data on heterogeneity test statistics on
d the input parameters in the dataset or by-group.  The output dataset
d can be listed to the Stata log, saved to a data frame, saved to a disk
d file, or written to memory, overwriting the existing dataset.
d Optionally, parmhet may also add variables to the existing dataset,
d containing inverse-variance weights and/or semi-weights and/or
d semi-weight-based standard errors.  These additional variables may
d then be input to the metaparm module of the parmest package, to
d produce summary meta-analysed parameter estimates, using the
d fixed-effect method or the DerSimonian-Laird randomly-variable-effect
d method.  parmiv is a routine intended for use by programmers, and
d inputs variables containing estimates, standard errors and
d (optionally) degrees of freedom, and outputs additional variables in
d the existing dataset, containing inverse-variance weights and/or
d semi-weights and/or semi-weight-based standard errors and/or
d heterogeneity test statistics for the dataset or by-group.
d
d Author: Roger Newson
d Distribution-Date: 16november2025
d Stata-Version: 16
f parmhet.ado
f parmiv.ado
f parmhet.sthlp
f parmhet_basic_opts.sthlp
f parmhet_resultsset_opts.sthlp
f parmhet_hettest_opts.sthlp
f parmhet_resultsset.sthlp
f parmiv.sthlp
f parmhet_example1.dta
e
